;;; PROPOSITION 4.7: a positive functional is bounded, ||phi|| = phi(1).
;;; The square root of 1 - x* x (Proposition 1.33 in the notes) is uiba-one-minus-sa-square
;;; (ba4-sqrt.scm), for ||x|| < 1; the bound for ||x|| <= 1 and then for all x follows by scaling.
;;;   pos-lf-unit         phi(1) in RR, 0 <= phi(1)
